    "body": "## What does this PR do?\n\nnvcc 13.x (CUDA 13+) rejects redeclaring a template parameter name as a local variable inside the function body. `apply_dequantization()` and `apply_selective_dequantization()` in `csrc/fp_quantizer/fp_quantize_impl.cu` both declare a local `constexpr int q_exponent_bits` that shadows the template parameter `int q_exponent_bits`, so building `fp_quantizer_op` on CUDA 13+ fails with:\n\n```\ncsrc/fp_quantizer/fp_quantize_impl.cu(234): error: template parameter \"q_exponent_bits\" may not be redeclared in this scope\ncsrc/fp_quantizer/fp_quantize_impl.cu(413): error: template parameter \"q_exponent_bits\" may not be redeclared in this scope\n2 errors detected in the compilation of \"csrc/fp_quantizer/fp_quantize_impl.cu\".\n```\n\nCUDA 12.x compilers accept the shadowing, which is why upstream CI has not caught it.\n\n## Why is this PR needed?\n\nPyTorch >= 2.12 headers require C++20, and DeepSpeed's `nvcc_args()` now passes `-std=c++20` on CUDA 12.5+/13+. On a CUDA 13 + recent torch stack (e.g. CUDA 13.4 / torch 2.14) the fp_quantizer kernel no longer compiles at all, breaking `op_builder` / `python setup.py install` / `python -m build` when `DS_BUILD_FP_QUANTIZER=1`.\n\n## Design\n\nRename the two shadowing locals to `new_qeb`. The template parameter name is kept because it is part of the kernel signature and referenced by call sites (including the `clip<...>` template arguments).\n\nBehavior is unchanged: the local always equals `total_q_bits - mantisa_bits - 1` (e.g. 3+2=6), which differs from the template default (4) anyway — the existing line 233/412 `quantized_bits = q_mantisa_bits + q_exponent_bits + 1` already implicitly relied on the shadowed value.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Reproduced the failure with the pre-fix file on CUDA 13.4 + torch 2.14.1 (`-std=c++20`): 2 errors, build fails.\n- With the fix, the file compiles cleanly (0 errors) under the same toolchain.\n- Full wheel build succeeds: `python -m build --wheel --no-isolation --config-setting=\"--build-option=build_ext\"` on an A100 (sm_80/86/89/120) host, CUDA 13.4, Python 3.12, torch 2.14.1.\n\nHardware: 2x NVIDIA A100-SXM4-80GB (sm_80) host, compile targets sm_80/86/89/120.",
