      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep packed width based on the source exponent**\n\nWhen `T` is BF16 (the Python API's supported dtype), `new_qeb` is 8, the destination BF16 exponent width, whereas an E4M3 input has `q_exponent_bits == 4`. This changes `quantized_bits` from 8 to 12 (and similarly mis-sizes q6/q12), so group offsets and scale loads no longer match the buffer produced and allocated using `q_bits`; later groups are read out of bounds and dequantization returns corrupted values. Keep this expression based on the template `q_exponent_bits`; the same regression is duplicated in `apply_selective_dequantization`.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L19-L19](https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/blob/c4ab93d5849cd26535521bdd0c8d535aed3e491e/AGENTS.md#L19-L19)\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
      "commit_id": "c4ab93d5849cd26535521bdd0c8d535aed3e491e",
      "created_at": "2026-10-12T09:35:18Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -230,11 +230,11 @@ __global__ void apply_dequantization(uint8_t* val, T* q_val, int group_size, int\n     constexpr uint32_t vector_size = quantization::access_granularity / sizeof(T);\n     int tidx = (blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x) * vector_size;\n \n-    constexpr int quantized_bits = q_mantisa_bits + q_exponent_bits + 1;\n-    constexpr int q_exponent_bits = total_q_bits - mantisa_bits - 1;\n+    constexpr int new_qeb = total_q_bits - mantisa_bits - 1;\n+    constexpr int quantized_bits = q_mantisa_bits + new_qeb + 1;",
